      "observed": "A 74LVC1G86 XOR gate (U8), powered from +3V3, is connected to the TMC2209 network. U8 pin 2 is tied to U6 pin 21 (OA2), a motor-phase output of a 24 V-powered TMC2209 driver, and also to pump connector H8 pin 2. U8 pin 1 is tied to U7 pin 20 (STDBY), and U8 pin 4 output drives U6 pin 9 (MS1/AD0).",
      "expected": "The intended TMC2209 dosing-pump driver network has no XOR gate. MS1/AD0 should be a fixed logic level (or stable UART address pin), and 3.3 V logic inputs should not be connected directly to motor-phase outputs that can swing to the 24 V driver supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"119\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad2)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"21\") (pinfunction \"OA2\") (pintype \"output\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"120\") (name \"Net-(U8-Pad4)\") (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"MS1/AD0\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "shared single-wire UART bus (`STEP_BUS`) plus individual STEP lines"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U8 can be overvolted or damaged because its input sees 24 V-capable motor-phase swings, and the XOR output makes U6's MS1/AD0 dynamic, corrupting its microstep/UART address and causing unpredictable dosing-pump control.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains an undocumented 74LVC1G86 XOR gate connected between 24 V motor-phase outputs and a 3.3 V TMC2209 configuration pin, which is a likely anomaly rather than a documented limitation."
}

